{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.SkewMonoidAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":40,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.torusEval_emb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.torusEval_emb","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L292-L298","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.torusEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.torusEval","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L279-L290","doc":"**Universal evaluation of the quantum torus.**  Given a semiring `R`, a\ncoefficient ring-hom `φ : A →+* R`, a unit `ℓ : Rˣ` (the image of `L`)\nand the twist compatibility `φ(y • a) · ℓ^y = ℓ^y · φ(a)` for every\nL-degree `y`, there is a ring-hom `T → R`.  A thin re-exposure of\n`liftNCRingHom` specialised to the L-degree group; the caller supplies\nthe crossed-product compatibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.funcModel_qWeyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.funcModel_qWeyl","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L267-L277","doc":"**q-Weyl relation in the function model.**  The shift and\nscalar-power operators satisfy `shiftFwd ∘ mulPow q = q • (mulPow q ∘\nshiftFwd)` — i.e. `L·M = q·M·L` on `ℕ → K`.  This exhibits the corpus's\ncolored-Jones tower operators as a genuine q-Weyl representation of the\nquantum torus (the `evaluation map to the function model`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.mulPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.mulPow","kind":"def","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L263-L265","doc":"The multiplication-by-`q^N` operator, `M`'s image in the function model\n(`m = q^N`, the corpus meridian convention): `(mulPow q J)(N) = q^N · J N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.shiftFwd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.shiftFwd","kind":"def","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L258-L261","doc":"The forward shift on colour towers, `L`'s image in the function model:\n`(shiftFwd J)(N) = J (N+1)` — the corpus `QDifferenceOperator` uses this\nvia `J (N + j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_eq_zero_of_topDeg_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_eq_zero_of_topDeg_lt","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L244-L251","doc":"**Coefficients above the top L-degree vanish** — the key fact the skew\ndivision uses to certify the remainder's degree drop. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L239-L242","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_zero","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L235-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L231-L233","doc":"**Top L-degree** of `f` (`⊥` for `0`): the largest exponent in\n`expSupport`.  This is the degree brick B3 divides down. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L227-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.mem_expSupport_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.mem_expSupport_iff","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L218-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L215-L216","doc":"The coefficient of `f` at L-degree `n` (the `L^n`-component). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.expSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.expSupport","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L212-L213","doc":"The set of `ℤ`-exponents (L-degrees) appearing in `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeff_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeff_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L206-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.monomial_mul_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.monomial_mul_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L198-L204","doc":"**The twisted monomial product law** (`ℤ`-exponent form of\n`single_mul_single`): `L^m a · L^n b = L^{m+n} (a · σᵐ b)`, where\n`σᵐ = (ofAdd m) •`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv_eq_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv_eq_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L196-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_eq_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_eq_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L195-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.monomial_zero_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.monomial_zero_left","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L192-L193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.monomial","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L189-L190","doc":"The `ℤ`-indexed monomial `L^n · a = single (ofAdd n) a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.support_single_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.support_single_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L172-L180","doc":"A single monomial `single n a` with `a ≠ 0` has support `{n}` — the\nL-degree of a monomial is its exponent (used by B2/B3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L162-L169","doc":"`L ≠ 0` (over a nontrivial coefficient ring): its `ofAdd 1` coefficient\nis `1 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeff_Lgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeff_Lgen","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L156-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeff_emb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeff_emb","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L151-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.qWeyl_eigen_commutation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.qWeyl_eigen_commutation","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L142-L147","doc":"**Eigen-commutation (the paper's `LM = c·ML`).**  If `M : A` is a\nσ-eigenvector, `σ(M) = c·M`, then `L·M = c·(M·L)` in the torus.  For the\nfigure-eight torus `c = q²` (paper `t²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv_mul_emb_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv_mul_emb_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L134-L140","doc":"The `L⁻¹` transpose of the commutation: `L⁻¹ · σ(a) = a · L⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_mul_emb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_mul_emb","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L126-L132","doc":"**q-Weyl commutation (skew relation), `L · a = σ(a) · L`.**  This is the\ndefining relation of the quantum torus: moving `L` past a coefficient\ntwists it by `σ`.  With `σ(M) = q²·M` it is the paper's `LM = q²ML`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.LUnit_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.LUnit_val","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L122-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.LUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.LUnit","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L115-L120","doc":"`L` is a unit of the quantum torus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv_mul_Lgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv_mul_Lgen","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L111-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_mul_Linv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen_mul_Linv","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L107-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Linv","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L104-L105","doc":"`L⁻¹`: the negative skew generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Lgen","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L101-L102","doc":"`L`: the positive skew generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.emb_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.emb_apply","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.emb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.emb","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L89-L97","doc":"The coefficient (M-side) embedding `A → T`, `a ↦ single 1 a` — a ring\nhomomorphism (`single 1` is multiplicative because `1 • b = b`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L84-L85","doc":"`σ 1 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_mul","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L80-L82","doc":"`σ` is multiplicative (it is a ring-automorphism action). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_def","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L77-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L73-L75","doc":"The σ-twist automorphism of the coefficient ring: the action of the\nL-degree generator `ofAdd 1`.  For the paper's torus `σ(M) = q²·M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.QuantumTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.QuantumTorus","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L66-L71","doc":"**The quantum torus** as the skew-Laurent ring `A[L^±; σ]`:\nfinitely-supported `ℤ → A` with the σ-twisted product.  Here `A = R[M^±]`\nis the M-coefficient ring and the L-degree group `Multiplicative ℤ` acts\nby the twist automorphism `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Ldeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.Ldeg","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorus.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The L-degree group: `Multiplicative ℤ`, additively the `L`-exponent. ","signatureChunk":0}]}